     1,
     "<div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dear community, <br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I am running a measurement invariance analysis in ordinal data (theta parameterization, identification based on Wu &amp; Estabrook, ordered indicators, scaled and shifted test statistic, robust se and DWLS estimator for all models). <br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">When using semTools::compareFit function the output of the Chi Square Difference test method Satorra 2000 derives to a different chi-square difference than the simple substraction of the standard Chi-Square values (also not the exact difference when using the scaled chi-squared values). <br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Here my code:<br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">library(semTools)<br>compareFit.metric.scalar.improv &lt;- compareFit(fit.metric.improv,fit.scalar.improv)<br>summary(compareFit.metric.scalar.improv)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Results: </span><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Cascadia Code&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.6667px;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(0,34,64);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\">Scaled Chi-Squared Difference Test (method = “satorra.2000”)\r\n\r\nlavaan-&gt;unknown():  \r\n   lavaan NOTE: The “Chisq” column contains standard test \r\n   statistics, not the robust test that should be reported \r\n   per model. A robust difference test is a function of two \r\n   standard (not robust) statistics.\r\n                    Df AIC BIC  Chisq Chisq diff Df diff Pr(&gt;Chisq)    \r\nfit.metric.improv 1112         4778.4                                  \r\nfit.scalar.improv 1172         6224.8     996.71      60  &lt; 2.2e-16 ***\r\n---\r\nSignif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1\r\n\r\n####################### Model Fit Indices ###########################\r\n                  chisq.scaled df.scaled pvalue.scaled rmsea.scaled cfi.scaled tli.scaled  srmr\r\nfit.metric.improv    5059.826†      1112          .000        .042†      .941†      .937† .063†\r\nfit.scalar.improv    6101.898       1172          .000        .045       .927       .925  .065 \r\n\r\n################## Differences in Fit Indices #######################\r\n                                      df.scaled rmsea.scaled cfi.scaled tli.scaled  srmr\r\nfit.scalar.improv - fit.metric.improv        60        0.004     -0.015     -0.012 0.002</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Cascadia Code&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.6667px;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(255,255,255);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(0,34,64);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Cascadia Code&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.6667px;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span></span></span></span></span><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I might misspecify the method of the difference test but could not find the right method bc mostly Satorra, 2000 is recommended. Any idea why the Chi Square Difference is not exactly the difference of the Chi Square values? Is this cause for concern?</span></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:Verdana\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:Verdana\" size=\"2\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I highly appreciate your input. </span></span></span></span></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:Verdana\" size=\"2\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></span></span></span></font></div><div><font style=\"font-family:Verdana\" size=\"2\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Best wishes and happy new year! </span></span></span></span></font></div><div><font size=\"4\"><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-moz-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Sans Serif\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\">